      },
      "text": "### Why 4f Orbitals Don't Shield"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-LANTHANIDES.md#010",
      "path": [
        "10-LANTHANIDES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:periodic-table:10-lanthanides, git-history:periodic-table:10-lanthanides]",
        "canonical_path": "periodic-table/10-LANTHANIDES.md",
        "concepts": "[lanthanides]",
        "current_path": "periodic-table/10-LANTHANIDES.md",
        "id": "maxim:periodic-table:lanthanides",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "periodic-table",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[lanthanides]",
        "section": "periodic-table",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Lanthanides - La through Lu (Z=57–71)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nNORMAL EXPECTATION: going right across a period, nuclear charge increases by 1 each step\n  → outer electron radius increases OR stays constant\n  → ionic radius should stay roughly constant across lanthanides if 4f shields as expected"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-LANTHANIDES.md#011",
      "path": [
        "10-LANTHANIDES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:periodic-table:10-lanthanides, git-history:periodic-table:10-lanthanides]",
        "canonical_path": "periodic-table/10-LANTHANIDES.md",
        "concepts": "[lanthanides]",
        "current_path": "periodic-table/10-LANTHANIDES.md",
        "id": "maxim:periodic-table:lanthanides",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "periodic-table",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[lanthanides]",
        "section": "periodic-table",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Lanthanides - La through Lu (Z=57–71)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS:\n  Ionic radius SHRINKS by ~17 pm across the series (La³⁺ → Lu³⁺)\n  This is LARGE — more than the difference between many periods"
    },
    {
      "id": "10-LANTHANIDES.md#012",
      "path": [
        "10-LANTHANIDES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:periodic-table:10-lanthanides, git-history:periodic-table:10-lanthanides]",
        "canonical_path": "periodic-table/10-LANTHANIDES.md",
        "concepts": "[lanthanides]",
        "current_path": "periodic-table/10-LANTHANIDES.md",
        "id": "maxim:periodic-table:lanthanides",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "periodic-table",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[lanthanides]",
        "section": "periodic-table",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Lanthanides - La through Lu (Z=57–71)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHY:\n  4f orbitals have their probability maximum INSIDE the 5s and 5p shells\n  The 4f electrons spend much of their time in the core region → poor screening\n  → Each successive 4f electron adds nuclear charge (+1 proton) but screens poorly\n  → Effective nuclear charge felt by outer electrons INCREASES across the series\n  → All outer orbital radii (5s, 5p, 5d, 6s) systematically contract"
    }
